You are debugging a production issue where a critical dependency resolution service hangs indefinitely, triggering thread starvation alerts under load. Thread dumps show dozens of worker threads stuck in `RUNNABLE` or `BLOCKED` states inside internal map methods. A recent PR introduced this implementation:

java
@Service
public class DependencyGraphService {
    private final Map<String, String> resolvedCache = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    public String resolveDependency(String node) {
        return resolvedCache.computeIfAbsent(node, key -> {
            String parent = extractParent(key);
            return parent != null ? resolveDependency(parent) + "->" + key : key;
        });
    }

    private String extractParent(String key) {
        int idx = key.lastIndexOf(':');
        return idx > 0 ? key.substring(0, idx) : null;
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where a batch-processing service processes customer orders using a custom collection implementation. The service executes inside a `@Transactional` boundary, but nested database updates within the collection processing step intermittently fail with `TransactionRequiredException`, and partial uncommitted states are observed:

java
@Service
public class OrderBatchService {
    @Autowired
    private OrderRepository orderRepository;

    @Transactional
    public void processPendingOrders(CustomBatchList<Order> orders) {
        orders.parallelStream().forEach(this::applyDiscountAndSave);
    }

    public void applyDiscountAndSave(Order order) {
        order.setDiscount(0.10);
        orderRepository.save(order);
    }
}
